{"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/covering\/graphprotocols\/graph\/lexicographicallyfirstminimumvertexcover()"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"lexicographicallyFirstMinimumVertexCover"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":"]"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"anchor":"discussion","level":2,"text":"Discussion","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"It is the complement of the lexicographically greatest maximum independent set, not of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"least one: the least vertex of a symmetric difference is in one cover exactly when it is in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the other cover’s complement. That set is found as in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"lexicographicallyFirstMaximumIndependentSet()"},{"type":"text","text":", with each choice the other way round: the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"core pass on a bipartite component leaves out each vertex it decides, a complete component"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"keeps its greatest vertex, and any other component deletes a vertex whenever a maximum set"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"without it remains, with the reductions taking a simplicial vertex greater than all its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"neighbours. The cost is that of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"lexicographicallyFirstMaximumIndependentSet()"},{"type":"text","text":": O(m √n) on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"bipartite components, and up to c exponential searches on a component of c vertices the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reductions do not settle. The search does not check for task cancellation."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/lexicographicallyFirstMinimumVertexCover()"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering","doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The lexicographically first minimum vertex cover: of the smallest vertex covers, the least"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"by vertex index (the rule of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"lexicographicallyFirstMaximumIndependentSet()"},{"type":"text","text":": of two covers"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of one size, the lesser holds the least vertex of their symmetric difference), in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order; [] for the empty graph. Every vertex with a self-loop is in it; parallel edges count"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"once."}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Instance Method","remoteSource":{"fileName":"ExactCovering.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Covering\/ExactCovering.swift#L1739"},"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"lexicographicallyFirstMinimumVertexCover"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":"]"}],"externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P8CoveringE40lexicographicallyFirstMinimumVertexCoverSay0G0QzGyF","modules":[{"relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"],"name":"Covering"}],"symbolKind":"method","extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","role":"symbol","title":"lexicographicallyFirstMinimumVertexCover()"},"references":{"doc://Covering/documentation/Covering/GraphProtocols/Graph":{"title":"Graph","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/covering\/graphprotocols\/graph","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"extension"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P","kind":"identifier","text":"Graph"}],"role":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Graph"}]},"doc://Covering/documentation/Covering/GraphProtocols":{"url":"\/documentation\/covering\/graphprotocols","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols","type":"topic","role":"collection","abstract":[],"title":"GraphProtocols"},"doc://Covering/documentation/Covering/GraphProtocols/Graph/lexicographicallyFirstMinimumVertexCover()":{"title":"lexicographicallyFirstMinimumVertexCover()","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/covering\/graphprotocols\/graph\/lexicographicallyfirstminimumvertexcover()","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"lexicographicallyFirstMinimumVertexCover"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":"]"}],"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The lexicographically first minimum vertex cover: of the smallest vertex covers, the least"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"by vertex index (the rule of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"lexicographicallyFirstMaximumIndependentSet()"},{"type":"text","text":": of two covers"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of one size, the lesser holds the least vertex of their symmetric difference), in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order; [] for the empty graph. Every vertex with a self-loop is in it; parallel edges count"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"once."}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/lexicographicallyFirstMinimumVertexCover()"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/Graph/Vertex":{"title":"Vertex","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/graph\/vertex","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"associatedtype"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SH","text":"Hashable"}],"role":"symbol","abstract":[],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Vertex"},"doc://Covering/documentation/Covering":{"url":"\/documentation\/covering","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering","type":"topic","role":"collection","abstract":[],"title":"Covering"}}}